## 4. CERSAI Bulk Download Request

Existing table:

```text
CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
```

The existing table contains, among other fields:

```text
CIF_NUMBER
CKYC_NUMBER
CKYC_REFERENCE_ID
MOBILE_NUMBER
REQ_UNIQUE_ID
REQ_INIT_CHANNEL_DATE
IS_DOWNLOADED_FLAG
MODIFIED_DATE
...
```

Add the three-state eligibility flag:

```sql
ALTER TABLE CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
    ADD (
        CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE CHAR(1)
            DEFAULT 'P'
            NOT NULL
    );
```

Add the state constraint:

```sql
ALTER TABLE CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
    ADD CONSTRAINT CK_CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE
    CHECK (CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE IN ('P', 'N', 'Y'));
```

Add an index for the Download JAR:

```sql
CREATE INDEX IDX_CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE
    ON CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
       (CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE);
```

### Existing-data migration

If the table already contains data, add the column first without `NOT NULL`:

```sql
ALTER TABLE CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
    ADD (
        CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE CHAR(1)
    );
```

Populate existing records according to their actual business state:

```sql
UPDATE CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
SET CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE = 'P'
WHERE CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE IS NULL;
```

Then enforce the default and constraint:

```sql
ALTER TABLE CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
    MODIFY (
        CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE CHAR(1)
            DEFAULT 'P'
            NOT NULL
    );

ALTER TABLE CKYCBULK.CERSAI_BULK_DOWNLOAD_REQUEST
    ADD CONSTRAINT CK_CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE
    CHECK (CERSAI_DOWNLOAD_ELIGIBLE IN ('P', 'N', 'Y'));
```

The correct initial value for a newly-created CERSAI download request is `P`.

