## 12. Oracle Scheduler

Example: run every 15 minutes.

```sql
BEGIN
    DBMS_SCHEDULER.CREATE_JOB (
        job_name        => 'CKYCBULK.JOB_EXPIRE_CERSAI_CONSENTS',
        job_type        => 'STORED_PROCEDURE',
        job_action      => 'CKYCBULK.PR_EXPIRE_CERSAI_CONSENTS',
        start_date      => SYSTIMESTAMP,
        repeat_interval => 'FREQ=MINUTELY;INTERVAL=15',
        enabled         => TRUE,
        auto_drop       => FALSE,
        comments        => 'Expires pending CERSAI consent windows and marks download requests eligible.'
    );
END;
/
```

The scheduler does not need to run exactly at the expiry time. It only needs to run frequently enough that the Download JAR sees the record as eligible before it performs its next run.

